\omega\\;R\\subseteq(\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma))^k\\times\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}rule} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{Rule}_S(R,\\Sigma)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists k\\in\\omega\\;R\\subseteq(\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma))^k\\times\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A rule <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R\">\\(R\\)</span> is a relation between <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span>-tuples of premises and a conclusion</li>\n<li>For MP: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k = 2\">\\(k = 2\\)</span> (two premises <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi, \\varphi \\to \\psi\">\\(\\varphi, \\varphi \\to \\psi\\)</span>)</li>\n<li>Side-conditioned rules may carry additional metadata; their concrete encodings are defined by the corresponding rule atoms.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch17/58-df-formula.md","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"./58-df-function-set.md","status":"resolved","id":"aa82947fba077a45","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[./58-df-function-set.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-formula.md","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\subseteq V$ (see [[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]).","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\Sigma,R\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"k\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\ma